  "body": "What happens:\n\nThe Finish3D parallel toolpath stops, picks up, or behaves unexpectedly over model holes. The land model (fill_openings) lids closed openings narrower than a stated width. But holes wider than the width, open holes, and holes at lid edges still cause stops and picks.\n\nExpected:\n\nThe Finish3D parallel toolpath should pass over holes as if they are not there. The tool should fly over every hole smoothly at a consistent height. No stops. No picks. No weird behavior over hole regions.\n\nDone means:\n\n- The Finish3D parallel path passes over all holes without retract or plunge moves over hole regions\n- No stops or picks over hole regions\n- The path verifies cleanly against the real model\n\nClassification (to be applied by a session with write access):\n\n- bug: wrong behaviour over holes in Finish3D parallel toolpath\n- P3: wrong behaviour with a workaround (enable fill_openings with a wide width)\n- area:3d: finishing3d crate, parallel strategy\n- effort:high: several crates, new behaviour with tests (safety floor - changes posted G-code)\n- source:agent: filed by an agent during the user's testing session\n\nLabels are set per AGENTS.md Issue Law; this session cannot set labels on NeoTech/Camcraft (FlamingFireCoding has push:false). A collaborator's session can apply the five labels above, then the issue is pickable in the bug lane.\n",
